#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Entity Model"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "Unified Entity Model (v0.8)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:8
msgid ""
"FreeAnima stores most structured business data in a single **`entities`** "
"table. Self layer remains physically isolated in [`self_blocks`](../"
"cognition/self-layer.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "Hierarchy: subject → world → content"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:16
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Layer       | Entity type     | Role                                                |\n"
"| ----------- | --------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| **Subject** | `agent`, `user` | Who acts — exists **before** and **outside** worlds |\n"
"| **World**   | `world`         | Logical namespace / permission boundary             |\n"
"| **Content** | `content`       | Business data (tasks, future memory components, …)  |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:18
msgid ""
"Subjects do **not** belong to a world. Each subject may have exactly **one "
"default private world** (exclusive, auto-created on subject creation). "
"Content belongs to a world via `world_id` and inherits that world's "
"visibility boundary."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:19
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two orthogonal classifications"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:25
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Layer           | Cardinality              | Purpose                                                    |\n"
"| --------------- | ------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| **Entity type** | 4 fixed values           | Architecture boundary: `content`, `world`, `agent`, `user` |\n"
"| **Components**  | Dynamic, many per entity | Functional markers: `task_list`, `task_item`, …            |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:27
msgid ""
"Component fields live in **`body` JSONB** at the top level. "
"**`primary_component`** records the creation entry (usually immutable); list "
"views route by primary component."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:28
#, no-wrap
msgid "`entities` table"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:43
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Column                          | Role                                                        |\n"
"| ------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| `id`                            | `bigint` identity — global numeric ID                       |\n"
"| `type`                          | One of four entity types                                    |\n"
"| `world_id`                      | Native owning World (FK → `entities.id`)                    |\n"
"| `components`                    | `text[]` component tags                                     |\n"
"| `primary_component`             | Main component for module routing                           |\n"
"| `title` / `summary` / `content` | Shared text columns (all components may use)                |\n"
"| `body`                          | JSONB component payload                                     |\n"
"| `pinned`                        | Entity-level pin（任意 component）                          |\n"
"| `reference_count`               | `[[anima:id]]` 引用权重和                                   |\n"
"| `tag_ids`                       | 关联 `primary_component=tag` 的 entity id 数组（per-World） |\n"
"| `created_at` / `updated_at`     | Timestamps                                                  |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:45
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Not in v0.8 bootstrap:** relationship table, World nesting/mount, graph DB (PostgreSQL AGE). Subject↔world grants live in `world_config.grants` (no separate permission table).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:46
#, no-wrap
msgid "Subject (`agent` / `user`)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:53
msgid ""
"Identity is **`type`** plus `agent_config` or `user_config` primary "
"component."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:53
msgid ""
"Subjects are **not** scoped by `world_id` in a membership sense; row "
"`world_id` stays at bootstrap root (`ENTITY_ROOT_WORLD_ID`) as a table "
"placeholder."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:53
msgid ""
"**`agent_config` / `user_config` body**: `default_private_world_id` — the "
"subject's single default private world (auto-created on subject create; "
"configurable from private worlds owned by the subject)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:53
msgid ""
"**Notifications** use subject entity ids as `recipient_id` (see "
"[`notifications.md`](../cognition/notifications.md)); ids come from boot-"
"time **`ResolvedWorldContext`** (and are persisted to "
"`habitat_runtime_config.worlds`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:53
msgid ""
"**Service API Token**（`service_api_tokens` 表）绑定 subject entity id；"
"Habitat REST/SAP/MCP 从 Bearer token 解析调用方身份。见 [`remote-access.md`]"
"(../ops/remote-access.md)。"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:54
#, no-wrap
msgid "Boot-time ensure (`worlds` config)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:57
msgid ""
"Habitat startup runs **`ensureWorldSubjects()`** once (after migrations, "
"before engine):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:64
msgid ""
"**Optional override**: if `habitat_runtime_config.worlds.user_subject_id` / "
"`agent_subject_id` (or legacy `notifications`) are set, ensures those entity "
"ids exist with the correct `type`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:64
msgid ""
"**Unconfigured**: discovers the lowest-id entity of `type=user` / "
"`type=agent`; if none exist, creates them with the next serial id (not fixed "
"`1`/`2`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:64
msgid ""
"Ensures each subject has a **default private world** "
"(`default_private_world_id`); private world ids are **not fixed**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:64
msgid ""
"If resolved ids differ from config (including when unset), **persists** them "
"back to `habitat_runtime_config.worlds` so the next boot is stable."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:64
msgid ""
"Binds **`ResolvedWorldContext`** in memory: `user_subject_id`, "
"`agent_subject_id`, `user_world_id`, `agent_world_id`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:64
msgid ""
"Type conflict (configured id exists but wrong `type`) **aborts service "
"startup**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:66
msgid ""
"Legacy SQL bootstrap seeds (public world id=1, Inbox id=2) are removed by "
"migration; default data is **code-owned**, not migration-seeded."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:67
#, no-wrap
msgid "World namespace"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:76
msgid ""
"**`type: world`** entities are logical containers (permission/list boundary)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:76
msgid "Visibility, owner, and grants live in **`world_config` body**:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:76
msgid "`private: false` — public world"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:76
msgid ""
"`private: true` + `owner_subject_id` — private world owned by an `agent` or "
"`user` entity"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:76
msgid ""
"`default_private: true` — marks the subject's **exclusive** default private "
"world (at most one per `owner_subject_id`)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:76
msgid ""
"`grants: [{ subject_id, permission: \"read\" | \"write\" }]` — explicit "
"subject grants (**write includes read**; `subject_id` must not equal owner). "
"Configured in Habitat Worlds UI; never hardcoded per subject in source."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:76
msgid "**Access rules** (MCP / LLM tools via `resolveToolWorld`):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:81
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  | World   | Read                   | Write                    |\n"
"  | ------- | ---------------------- | ------------------------ |\n"
"  | public  | all subjects           | owner **or** write grant |\n"
"  | private | owner **or** any grant | owner **or** write grant |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:84
msgid ""
"Owner always has full access without a grant row. Cross-world tool calls "
"must use grants — open-source builds must not special-case subject ids."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:84
msgid ""
"Do not confuse with semantic memory **`type=world`** (fact classification in "
"[`memory.md`](../cognition/memory.md)) — that becomes "
"`body.memory_kind=world` after future migration."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <messages><msg>
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:85 messages/po4a/en.xml:355
#: messages/po4a/en.xml:406
#, no-wrap
msgid "Content"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:89
msgid ""
"**`world_id`** is the sole namespace key; access boundary is inherited from "
"the owning world."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:89
msgid "Content entities do not store a separate owner column."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:90
#, no-wrap
msgid "UI location: Anima URI"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:93
msgid ""
"Shell UI locates entities with **Anima URI** (`anima:{id}?component=…`), not "
"by storing URI strings in PG. FK fields remain numeric ids (e.g. "
"`task_item_id`). Omitting `component` defaults to this entity’s "
"`primary_component` when opening. See [`anima-uri.md`](anima-uri.md) — "
"especially **Layering vs persistence**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:94
#, no-wrap
msgid "Task module (first consumer)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:97
msgid "TickTick-style lists and items map to:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:103
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Concept     | Entity         | Component      |\n"
"| ----------- | -------------- | -------------- |\n"
"| Task domain | `type=world`   | `world_config` |\n"
"| List        | `type=content` | `task_list`    |\n"
"| Item (task) | `type=content` | `task_item`    |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:105
msgid ""
"Items reference their list via `body.list_id` (entity id). Task items store "
"**title** and **content** on entity columns; **tags** 使用顶层 `tag_ids`（指"
"向同 World 的 `tag` entity，见下节）。各模块遗留的 `body.tags` 字符串数组不再"
"作为任务试点读写路径。Each world gets a **default list** (`is_default: "
"true`, name e.g.「收件箱」) **lazily** on first task use "
"(`ensureDefaultTaskListForWorld`); it cannot be deleted or archived but may "
"be renamed. List **`body.closed: true`** means archived: hidden from the "
"main sidebar by default (`tasklist.list` unless `include_closed`), "
"restorable via `tasklist.patch({ closed: false })`; contained task items are "
"kept."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:107
msgid ""
"Task/list **LLM 工具**默认在 **agent subject 专属 private world** 操作，多数"
"调用可省略 `world_id`；按 `id` / `list_id` 操作时从实体反查 world 并校验 "
"caller 权限。**MCP** 工具默认 scope 为 token 绑定 subject 的 private world。"
"Shell SAP/REST 仍通过 `subject_kind` 选择 user/agent world（见下表）。"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:109
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Folders** (`body.is_folder: true`) are container nodes in the sidebar tree only — they cannot hold tasks directly (`tasklist.item.create` / `task.moveToList` reject `list_id` pointing at a folder). Child lists and sub-folders reference a parent folder via `body.parent_id` (entity id of a folder, or omitted/null at root). Nesting must not form cycles. **Folders cannot be archived** — only deleted. Deleting a folder recursively removes all sub-folders and moves every contained list to root (`parent_id: null`); list task items are kept. List **`body.closed: true`** means archived (lists only): hidden from the main sidebar by default (`tasklist.list` unless `include_closed`), restorable via `tasklist.patch({ closed: false })` only; **any other mutation on an archived list or its tasks** (rename, move, edit, complete, …) returns `清单已归档`. Deleting a non-folder list removes its task items when `cascade` is true (default). `sort_order` is scoped among siblings sharing the same `parent_id`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:111
msgid ""
"LLM ToolSets: `@freeanima/feature-task/domain` — `task` (item CRUD + "
"`task_search`) and `tasklist` (list CRUD + `tasklist_search`); load via "
"`toolset_load`. `task_search` searches all lists when `list_id` is omitted. "
"Legacy `tasks` table and `/api/tasks/*` are removed after one-time migration "
"([`scripts/archive/migrate-tasks-to-entities.ts`](../../scripts/archive/"
"migrate-tasks-to-entities.ts))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:112
#, no-wrap
msgid "Shell UI: global Subject scope"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:115
msgid ""
"Habitat startup binds **`ResolvedWorldContext`** "
"(`createTypedHabitatClient().call(\"worlds.context\")` / `GET /rpc/v1/worlds/"
"context`). The product shell exposes a **single User / Agent toggle** in the "
"module header — not an arbitrary `world_id` picker. Selection maps to "
"`user_world_id` / `agent_world_id` and persists in `sessionStorage` for the "
"tab."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:125
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Surface          | World binding                                    | Control                        |\n"
"| ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------ |\n"
"| Shell header     | `user_world_id` or `agent_world_id`              | global **User / Agent** toggle |\n"
"| `/tasks`         | follows shell scope via SAP `subject_kind`       | none (inherits header)         |\n"
"| `/projects`      | follows shell scope via SAP `subject_kind`       | none (inherits header)         |\n"
"| `/email`         | follows shell scope via SAP `subject_kind`       | none (inherits header)         |\n"
"| `/notifications` | `recipient_kind` + subject entity id             | none (inherits header)         |\n"
"| `/diary`         | subject default private world via `subject_kind` | none (inherits header)         |\n"
"| `/vault`         | default **user** library; optional Agent view    | User: master password lock     |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:127
msgid ""
"SAP task/email methods accept optional `subject_kind` (defaults: task "
"`user`, email `agent`). Satellites read the shell scope via "
"**`useSubjectScope()`** from `@freeanima/client/portal-sdk`; Habitat REST "
"entity search uses **`resolveWorldIdForSubject()`** with the same scope."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:129
msgid ""
"Future multi-world browse (e.g. diary calendar aggregation across worlds) "
"should add **module-scoped** filters or Habitat tooling — not a speculative "
"arbitrary world picker."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:130
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tag module（轻语义）"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:133
msgid ""
"标签是独立 content entity，**per-World 扁平池**（无 scope/命名空间、无层级、"
"无全局池）："
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:137
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Concept | Entity         | Component |\n"
"| ------- | -------------- | --------- |\n"
"| Tag     | `type=content` | `tag`     |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:147
msgid "**名称**在 entity `title`；body 仅 `sort_order` / `client_op_id`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:147
msgid ""
"任意 content entity 通过顶层 **`tag_ids`** 挂载标签；含义由「实体类型 + 标"
"签」组合自然产生（不做语义空间区分）"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:147
msgid ""
"同 World 内 title（trim 后）唯一；删除标签时从该 World 所有实体的 `tag_ids` "
"剔除"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:147
msgid ""
"**Habitat RPC：** `tag.list` / `tag.search` / `tag.suggest` / `tag.create` / "
"`tag.patch` / `tag.delete` / `tag.setOnEntity`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:147
msgid ""
"**LLM ToolSet：** `tag`（`tag_list` / `tag_search` / `tag_create` / "
"`tag_update` / `tag_delete` / `tag_set_on_entity`）"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:147
msgid ""
"**搜索：** `EntitySearchOpts.tag_ids`（或 `task_item` filters.`tag_ids`）为数"
"组包含过滤（AND）"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:147
msgid ""
"**挂标签 UI：** 共享 `TagPicker`（`features/tag/ui`）— 常用（`tag.suggest` 按"
"目标实体 `primary_component` 频次）+ 搜索（`tag.search`）+ 新建；日记条目 / "
"日记块 / 任务详情共用"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:147
msgid ""
"**列表筛选 UI：** 任务/项目等本地 FilterBar（从当前列表收集已有 tag chips），"
"**不是**挂标签交互，不接入 `TagPicker`、不暴露新建"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:147
msgid ""
"**兼容：** `diary.suggestTags` 仍可用，内部委托同一频次查询（固定 "
"`diary_entry`）"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:148
#, no-wrap
msgid "Project module (v1 spec)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:151
msgid ""
"Project management uses a **separate folder tree** from task-list folders. "
"Tasks belong to either the task module (Backlog, `project_id` null) or "
"exactly one project — not both in UI at once."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:156
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Concept        | Entity         | Component        |\n"
"| -------------- | -------------- | ---------------- |\n"
"| Project folder | `type=content` | `project_folder` |\n"
"| Project        | `type=content` | `project`        |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:158
msgid ""
"`task_item.body.project_id` links items to a project. Optional project "
"background notes use entity `content` (not `body`). Smart Lists in the task "
"module default to tasks with no `project_id`. Shell route `/projects`; "
"Habitat RPC `projectfolder.*`, `project.*`, `project.item.*`；跨边界归属用 "
"`task.moveToProject` / `task.moveToList`。"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:160
msgid "Full spec: [`docs/modules/project.md`](../modules/project.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:161
#, no-wrap
msgid "Email module (Estate)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:164
msgid "Email accounts, threads, and mirrored messages map to:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:170
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Concept | Entity         | Component       |\n"
"| ------- | -------------- | --------------- |\n"
"| Account | `type=content` | `email_account` |\n"
"| Thread  | `type=content` | `email_thread`  |\n"
"| Message | `type=content` | `email_message` |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:172
msgid ""
"Accounts store SMTP/IMAP settings and sync cursor in `body.sync`. Messages "
"store IMAP UID in `body.imap_uid`; human-readable subject uses entity "
"`title`. Sync pipeline: RFC822 → CTE/charset decode → strip attachments to "
"disk → store **decoded content raw** in entity `content` (`text/plain` or "
"`text/html`, see `body.content_type`); pure text always in `body.text` "
"(preview / ToolSet default). Do **not** keep the full RFC822 blob on the "
"entity. `email_read` / `email.message.read`: default body = plain text; "
"`raw=true` = content raw (html or plain). UI sandboxes `text/html` via iframe"
"（默认白底）. Also returns `headers`（SMTP/MIME map，小写键；不含已在实体字段"
"中的 From/To/Subject/Date）and `attachments`（落盘于 `FREEANIMA_HOME/email-"
"attachments/{account_id}/{message_id}/`，元信息在 `body.attachments`）. "
"Shell sidebar mirrors common mail apps: Inbox (`direction=inbound`, unread/"
"all) vs Sent (`direction=outbound`, no unread filter). `email_search` "
"supports optional `from` / `sent_after` / `sent_before`（AND with query）. "
"IMAP sync upserts threads/messages; UI lives in shell `/email` (SAP "
"`email.*` methods), not Habitat REST."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:174
msgid ""
"LLM ToolSets: `@freeanima/feature-email/domain` — `email-account` (account "
"entities) and `email` (sync, send/receive, search); load via `toolset_load`. "
"User and agent each have accounts in their **default private world**; LLM "
"tools accept optional **`world_id`** (SAP uses `subject_kind`). Legacy "
"`config.yaml` `email.accounts[]` migrates via [`scripts/archive/migrate-"
"email-to-entities.ts`](../../scripts/archive/migrate-email-to-entities.ts)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:175
#, no-wrap
msgid "Diary module"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:178
msgid "Structured journal entries for **user** and **agent** subjects:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:182
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Concept | Entity         | Component     |\n"
"| ------- | -------------- | ------------- |\n"
"| Entry   | `type=content` | `diary_entry` |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:184
msgid ""
"Entries live in each subject's **`default_private_world_id`**. "
"`body.entry_at` is the timeline sort key; optional top-level **`tag_ids`**"
"（指向同 World 的 `tag` entity；历史 `body.tags` 字符串已迁移剥离）。**Body "
"text lives in child `content_block` rows** (`block_type: text`, `parent_id` "
"→ entry); the container entity `content` column is unused (empty after one-"
"shot migration)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/product/entity-model.md:188
msgid ""
"**SAP:** `diary.*` + `diary.block*` — all take `subject_kind: user | agent`. "
"`diary.append` adds a new text block; `diary.patch` updates metadata only; "
"delete cascades blocks."
msgstr ""

